// Dynamics (Nov 2026): every built-in piece plays its dynamics. The Mutopia pieces are compiled with LilyPond's Dynamic_performer
// at Staff level, so the marks the edition writes in any voice or in its Dynamics line reach the notes (the Entertainer's,
// Clair de lune's, Beethoven's Fifth's were lost before). Three editions write (almost) none — Für Elise has only its pp,
// the Toccata and the Promenade none — so they carry editorial dynamics in the usual performance (Für Elise: pp, the B section
// p→f, the C section pp→f and to ff at its arpeggios; the Toccata: ff, the prestissimo f, mf passages, fff at the close;
// the Promenade: f, mf→ff mid-way, ff to the end).
